      "actor": "main-agent",
      "reason": "Necessary transitive closure of the brand rename, in four groups, none of which could be foreseen at PLAN time because the scope contract was derived from checklist Files declarations before the rename surface was fully measured. (1) packages/utils/src/handlers/{aux-doc,auxiliary,tool-status,truth}.ts - user-facing runtime strings that instructed the OLD bin name; leaving them would ship a CLI that teaches lattice while its docs say proof-or-stop, and packages/utils/src is now a gated brand-check root so they would also fail the gate. (2) packages/main/tests/{b90d6-init-dispatch-guidance,milestone-status}.test.mjs and scripts/verify-{codex-assets,global-lab-entrypoint}.mjs - assertions that PINNED the old brand literals; each was repinned to the new expected value, never deleted or weakened, because a rename that passes only by disabling its own assertions is not a rename. (3) scripts/verify-brand-gate-negative.mjs and scripts/verify-done-suite-green.mjs - NEW verifiers created because the DEV->REVIEW gate correctly REFUSED two non-mechanical attestations; they turn 'the brand gate bites' and 'the DONE suite is green' into executable receipts. (4) These additions are why the gate now has mechanical evidence instead of prose. All 13 signature salts, CHANGELOG.md and every foreign story archive remain byte-unchanged; root npm test is green (REAL_EXIT=0, 0 failure lines).",
